{{- /*
  github/pr-comments — canonical spawn payload for delegating unresolved PR
  review threads to a child conversation. Consumed by babysit-my-prs and
  babysit-this-pr. Extracted per mitto-g61.8; pre-conditions the caller sets:
    - <number>, <title>, <owner/repo>, <count>, <headRefName>, <baseRefName>,
      <PR_HEAD>, <WORKING_MODE>, <WORKING_PATH>, <PENDING_FEEDBACK_JSON> populated by
      the surrounding fetch + working-copy-decision blocks.
    - {{ .Session.ID }} required — self_id: is emitted directly.
*/ -}}
mitto_conversation_new(self_id: "{{ .Session.ID }}",
  title: "Address review comments on PR #<number>: <title>",
  initial_prompt: "PR #<number> (<title>) in <owner/repo> has <count> pending feedback items.

    Working-copy mode: <WORKING_MODE>  ('local' = reuse repo path as-is;
                                          'worktree' = create a fresh worktree, do NOT touch the main checkout)
    Repo path:         <WORKING_PATH>
    PR branch:         <headRefName>   (head commit <PR_HEAD>)
    Base branch:       <baseRefName>

    PR author: <PR_AUTHOR_LOGIN>
    Verified user-owned accounts and identity evidence: <VERIFIED_USER_IDENTITY>
    Pending items with full discussions, author types, IDs/URLs and timestamps:
    <PENDING_FEEDBACK_JSON>
    Prior decisions, objections, reaffirmations, and agent-posted reply IDs:
    <FEEDBACK_CHECKPOINT>
    Collection procedure:
    <copy the full shared collection procedure above, including queries and pagination checks>

    {{ template "github/shared/pr-feedback-policy" . }}

    {{ template "github/shared/pr-feedback-checkpoint" . }}

    Before acting, refresh all feedback sources for this same PR (full thread
    discussions, general comments, review summaries, with pagination) using the
    shared collection procedure. Reconcile newer author direction, including a
    general comment superseding a supplied thread request. Retain the delegated
    work scope; report unrelated new requests to the parent for its next run.
    Do not expand to other PRs or implement a superseded request.
    Inherit the parent's interaction mode, not the child's one-off status:
    {{- if and .Session.IsLoop (not .Session.IsLoopForced) }}
    unattended — only mitto_ui_notify, never interactive UI; defer blocked items.
    {{- else }}
    interactive — use Mitto UI if a blocking clarification is needed.
    {{- end }}

    For EACH actionable request you MUST do exactly one of:
      (a) Apply a code fix that addresses the comment, then reply to the
          discussion on the PR referencing the pushed commit that fixed it.
      (b) Reply to the thread with a concrete reason it will not be fixed
          (e.g., 'out of scope for this PR — filed as beads mitto-XXX',
          'disagree with reviewer because <reason>', 'already addressed in
          commit abc123', etc.).
    A material objection to an author request awaits clarification, not automatic
    rejection. Do not repeat a substantive reply already recorded for this item.
    Never silently skip a request. Acknowledgments/status-only comments need no
    reply. Never mark a thread resolved without a verified fix.

    Working-copy rules:
      - If 'local': operate directly in the given repo path. Never leave
        uncommitted files behind; if anything is dirty at start, abort and
        switch to worktree mode.
      - If 'worktree': create a fresh worktree with
          git -C <WORKING_PATH> fetch origin <headRefName>
          TMPDIR=\$(mktemp -d) && git -C <WORKING_PATH> worktree add \"\$TMPDIR\" origin/<headRefName>
        Do all edits inside \$TMPDIR. Never modify files under
        <WORKING_PATH> itself; the user may be working there.

    To post a reply on a review thread, use the GraphQL addPullRequestReviewThreadReply mutation
    (or 'gh api /repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/{number}/comments' with in_reply_to=<thread's first comment id>).
    To mark it resolved, use the resolveReviewThread mutation with the thread id from the JSON.
    General comments and review summaries have no resolvable thread: reply with
    a PR comment linking the source URL, never invent a review-thread ID.

    Local gate before pushing: run the project's format → lint → unit → integration
    steps (whatever the repo's Makefile or docs specify) and only push once
    they all pass. Force-push with --force-with-lease.

    When done, resolve only fixed review threads; leave blocked/disputed ones
    unresolved. Report back per item: published, pending-push, replied-only, awaiting-author, or
    superseded, plus the updated PR feedback checkpoint. The parent must recover
    this report before deciding that these comment versions have been handled.",
  acp_server: <prefer "coding" or "fast" tagged server>)
